Ha — the OLD code "worked" here via exactly the defect being fixed (any non-empty capture passes). The CORRECT fix for the TEST mock: make the default ls-remote response branch-aware. The default mock knows the branch only as 'bug/PROJ-123'... but for this test the expected branch is ai/gh-1420. Make the default mock parse the branch from the command:

```js
if (args.command.indexOf('git ls-remote --heads origin') === 0) {
    var probed = args.command.substring('git ls-remote --heads origin '.length);
    return '9a7e2aec...\trefs/heads/' + probed + '\n';
}
```

That mirrors real git faithfully (the probe asks for branch X → ref line for X). Apply to the default mock in loadPushReworkChangesForAction.

